QASP – Quantum Agent Software Package: a Python research software package providing reusable components and integrated workflows for quantum reinforcement learning, quantum classifiers, quantum kernels, generative learning and combinatorial optimisation. QASP supports differentiable hybrid quantum-classical workflows and execution through local and distributed simulation environments.

This software is authored by: André Manuel Sequeira

This program makes use and is distributed with the following libraries: * Gymnasium: (https://github.com/Farama-Foundation/Gymnasium) * Matplotlib: (https://github.com/matplotlib/matplotlib) * NumPy: (https://github.com/numpy/numpy) * pandas: (https://github.com/pandas-dev/pandas) * PennyLane: (https://github.com/PennyLaneAI/pennylane) * Ray / RLlib: (https://github.com/ray-project/ray) * SciPy: (https://github.com/scipy/scipy) * TensorDict: (https://github.com/pytorch/tensordict) * PyTorch: (https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch) * TorchRL: (https://github.com/pytorch/rl) * ipykernel: (https://github.com/ipython/ipykernel) * pytest: (https://docs.pytest.org/) * Ruff: (https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff) * scikit-learn: (https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn) * NetworkX: (https://github.com/networkx/networkx) * nbformat: (https://github.com/jupyter/nbformat) * Weights & Biases SDK: (https://github.com/wandb/wandb)

